"""Name the model set and choose how scoring results are published.

Bundle setup offers defaults for every destination; entering a name overrides
that default. Catalog, schema and deployment suffix are added automatically.
model_name is the registered model set; prediction_table stores its results.

multi_model.py defines each target, model, training/CV, preprocessing and quality
limits. This file groups those models into one release and chooses promotion
and scoring destinations. For revenue and cost models, approve both together
here; define the profit calculation (revenue - cost) in features/scoring.py.

promotion_policy applies to the COMPLETE set. automatic checks each branch's
saved quality_threshold, quality_gates and min_improvement from multi_model.py.
All branches must pass absolute gates and none may regress on its selected metric.
At least one branch must improve by its min_improvement (a positive gain is required
even when min_improvement=0); equal peers may join that release. Otherwise the
candidate remains available and the previous champion stays active. The first set
needs absolute thresholds.
manual_approval uses the same quality checks when approve is requested.
Each replacement is compared with the corresponding model in the champion set,
not independently moved component aliases. An all-tied set does not pass. Scoring is a
separate job. Set score_handoff="after_alias_change" in config/workflow.json
and redeploy matching job definitions to start it after a successful automatic
promotion, manual approval or rollback. With disabled, run/schedule score
independently. Pending approval, failed gates and reject never trigger handoff.
Changing quality settings requires a newly trained set.

Each complete candidate becomes challenger; a later candidate moves it to
previous_challenger. Approve activates the set and clears its challenger alias.
Reject records rejection_reason and blocks approval, keeping the candidate
visible until replaced. previous_champion supports whole-set rollback.

Output modes (example: revenue and cost models, profit = revenue - cost):
- all: one table holds id, revenue prediction, cost prediction and profit.
  Each model's own scoring outputs are included too. This is the default.
- combined_only: the models still run, but the table holds id and profit;
  intermediate model predictions/outputs are not saved. Active combined rules
  must have been captured in the approved set; an empty rule list is an error.
- separate_views: the physical table holds everything, as in all. Model views
  expose each selected model's columns; the combined view exposes profit.
  Views read the same committed data and do not store independent copies.
Every mode retains record keys, relevant statuses and model-set provenance.

Output selection does not change the batch policy in config/workflow.json:
- incremental_append keeps earlier predictions when a new model set is selected
  and uses the new set for newly inserted source rows.
- full_rebuild rebuilds the full source snapshot when the selected set changes.

source_change_policy below handles source corrections independently:
- reject (default): updating/deleting an existing source row fails the batch.
- rebuild_on_change: UPDATE/DELETE triggers the existing full-rebuild scorer,
  even with the same set. All current rows are scored with the selected set,
  including both model and combined rules. Deleted rows disappear; lag/rolling
  history is rebuilt. This replaces all earlier results, including predictions
  from older model versions. No training occurs. Inserts alone still append.
  Local inference requires the full snapshot to fit max_rows/max_input_mb.
  Spark inference keeps the snapshot distributed; those limits still bound training.
  Permission errors still fail; they are not corrections. Expired CDF history
  fails unless auto_rebuild_on_cdf_expiry=true enables recovery of recognized
  history loss as a separate scoring policy.

Rule exceptions fail the job before publishing new results. Previous successful
results remain. Changing all/combined_only storage schemas needs a new table.
"""


def build_model_set():
    """Choose where results are published; business rules live in features/scoring.py."""
    enabled = {{if eq .training_layout "multi_target"}}True{{else}}False{{end}}
    if not enabled:
        return None
    return {
        "promotion_policy": "{{.model_set_promotion_policy}}",
        # Registry object: groups the component models under one approved version.
        "model_name": "{catalog}.{metadata_schema}.{{if .model_set_name}}{{.model_set_name}}{{else}}{{.project_name}}_set{{end}}{resource_suffix}",
        # Physical Delta output: custom name from setup, or the project default.
        "prediction_table": "{catalog}.{output_schema}.{{if .model_set_table_name}}{{.model_set_table_name}}{{else}}{{.project_name}}_set_scores{{end}}{resource_suffix}",
        "combined_rules_path": "../features",
        # A correction may replace all results even with incremental_append.
        # Legacy projects without this setting keep the reject behavior.
        "source_change_policy": "{{.source_change_policy}}",
        "publication": {
            # all: persist model and combined results in one physical table.
            # combined_only: compute models, persist only combined values and
            # keys/status/provenance. Requires active saved combined rules.
            # separate_views: persist all results once; expose named projections.
            "mode": "{{.model_set_output_mode}}",
{{if eq .model_set_output_mode "separate_views"}}
            # None creates a view for every branch. A mapping selects only its
            # listed branches and gives each a custom name; {} selects none.
            # Example: {"revenue": "{catalog}.{output_schema}.revenue_predictions{resource_suffix}"}
            "model_views": None,
            "model_view_template": "{catalog}.{output_schema}.{{if .model_view_prefix}}{{.model_view_prefix}}{{else}}{{.project_name}}_predictions{{end}}_{branch}{resource_suffix}",
            # Created only when the saved set has combined business outputs.
            "combined_view": "{catalog}.{output_schema}.{{if .combined_view_name}}{{.combined_view_name}}{{else}}{{.project_name}}_business_results{{end}}{resource_suffix}",
{{end}}
        },
    }
